// @trap cannot be called in this context
// The threads proposal traps `memory.atomic.wait32` on a memory that is not `shared`:
// with no other thread able to notify it, the wait could never end. V8 reports it as
// "Atomics.wait cannot be called in this context", wasmtime as "atomic wait on
// non-shared memory". Waiting across threads belongs to a shared-memory build.
print(__atomic_wait32__(16, 0, 0 as i64))
